  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ConcatenateBuffers",
    "file": "arrow/cpp/src/arrow/buffer.cc",
    "description": "`ConcatenateBuffers` sums `buffer->size()` into `out_length` and then calls `memcpy(..., buffer->size())` without validating that each input buffer size is non-negative. In this PoV, malformed IPC dictionary-delta data causes a sliced value buffer with a negative length to be produced upstream during array concatenation, and that negative `size()` is passed to `memcpy`, triggering ASan `negative-size-param`.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzed IPC stream input reaches `RecordBatchStreamReaderImpl::ReadInitialDictionaries` -> `ReadDictionary` -> `DictionaryMemo::AddDictionaryDelta`, which concatenates existing and delta dictionaries (`Concatenate`). For variable-width/binary dictionary values, crafted offsets/ranges can yield a `Buffer` slice with negative length; when `ConcatenateImpl::Visit(BinaryType)` calls `ConcatenateBuffers` on those value buffers, the unchecked negative `buffer->size()` is used as a memcpy length, causing the crash."
  },
